🐛 Bug
With our pre-Trained CNN model, we have input of different sizes.
We use torch::jit::load(model_file); to load the model. And do inference with libtorch on GPU.
This works fine on libtorch v1.6.
But inference turns out very slow on v1.8.1.
Upon further investigation, we found that only the first 21 loops were abnormal.
the detail is shown below: (abnormal loops cost more than 3 seconds)
